.TITLE "sudo"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Executes a command as another user. It typically grants __administrative privileges__ to perform tasks that require root access while maintaining an audit trail.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**sudo command**
Runs a specific command with root privileges.
> __command__ the target tool

**sudo -i**
Opens an interactive login shell with root environment and permissions.
> __-i__ interactive flag

**sudo -u user command**
Runs a command as a specified user instead of root.
> __-u__ user flag | __user__ target username

**sudo -k**
Invalidates the user's cached credentials, requiring a password for the next call.
> __-k__ kill cache flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __sudo__ allows for fine-grained control over administrative tasks without needing to log in as the root user. On macOS, the first user account created is automatically added to the __sudoers__ list with full privileges.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:passwd** **mac:whoami**

